    "label": {
      "en": "Income tax: higher tax rate"
    },
    "short_label": {
      "en": "$tin_high_rate"
    },
    "description": {
      "en": "Represents the higher rate of Irish income tax, 40%, applied to income above the standard-rate band. It is used in tin_ie's ArithOp for income taxed at the higher rate, in the SchedCalc tax schedule exposed on the web interface (Band_Rate), and -- serving a second purpose -- as the Marginal Relief rate in the BenCalc computing adjusted tax liability under the low-income exemption for those aged 65+. The Country Report confirms the higher rate stayed at 40% through 2022-2025 (Table 15) and that the Marginal Relief rate is likewise 40% (Table 11), consistent with a single constant serving both roles."
    },
